Description: renames the visible brand strings in winecfg (About dialog,
window title) from "Wine" to "Virtual". Purely cosmetic, does not break any API.

NOTE: example/template file. The exact context (line numbers, resource strings)
depends on the chosen WINE_TAG. Before enabling it, check it against the source
that was actually cloned:

    cd thirdparty/wine
    git grep -n "Wine configuration" programs/winecfg

Then adapt this file, rename it to patches/0001-branding-virtual.patch (without
.example) and run build-wine.sh again. build-wine.sh checks every patch with
`git apply --check` and skips it cleanly if it does not fit.

--- a/programs/winecfg/winecfg.rc
+++ b/programs/winecfg/winecfg.rc
@@
-    IDS_WINECFG_TITLE  "Wine configuration"
+    IDS_WINECFG_TITLE  "Virtual configuration"
@@
-    IDS_ABOUT          "Wine"
+    IDS_ABOUT          "Virtual (auf Wine-Basis, LGPL)"
